# --- Private. Never commit anything below this line. ---
#
# This repo is public. `pro/` used to sit below this line; it is published now, under PolyForm
# Strict 1.0.0 (see `pro/LICENSE`). What remains here is the measurement corpus and the working
# notes: real handwriting transcripts live under `.scratch/`, with employer ticket ids and
# colleagues' names in them. Publishing one is not repairable.
#
# This file is no longer the only protection. Three checks read the same list, and none of them
# reads it from HERE -- it lives in `scripts/private-paths.mjs`, on purpose, so that editing this
# file disarms nothing:
#
#   .githooks/pre-commit      refuses to stage a private path
#   .githooks/pre-push        refuses the whole history being pushed, not just the tip
#   scripts/private-gate.mjs  gate 0 in CI and at release -- the one `--no-verify` cannot reach
#
# The hooks need `core.hooksPath` set; `npm install` does it. All three run after the fact, so the
# lines below are still what keeps the mistake from being made.
#
# `git add -A` and `git commit -a` respect these rules. `git add -f` does NOT -- except where the
# folder is a nested git repo (`.scratch/`, `tools/`), which stages nothing at all. Do not
# force-add anything below, and do not delete a line to "just check something".

.scratch/
.scratch-inspect/
.claude/
docs/agents/
Claude.md
PRD.md
skills-lock.json
tools/

# Local research notes, not part of the repo
docs/research/reddit-research-access.md

# The content patterns gate 0 matches against. They ARE the strings being protected -- an employer
# name, a ticket prefix -- so committing them would publish exactly what they guard. CI reads them
# from the PRIVATE_CONTENT_PATTERNS secret instead.
.private-patterns
